  "text": "The programme is notable for its integration of social science and mātauranga Māori, ensuring community relevance and benefit. It employs probabilistic and scenario-based models to forecast landslides, linking triggering scenarios to susceptibility and impact analysis via RiskScape, and quantifying socio-economic consequences using the MERIT tool. The initiative is supported by a multi-institutional consortium and international expertise, and is recognized within the national professional community.",
